# Every image in docker-compose.yml builds with the repo root as its context (`context: .`), so
# without this file the whole tree is sent to the daemon on every build. tests/fixtures/ is
# test-only data — the sourcemap fixture bundle of sentinel-sourcemaps §13 (its two Vite builds,
# their maps, the generators, and a node_modules under app/ once someone rebuilds it) — that no
# Dockerfile COPYs on purpose and no service reads at runtime; the Go and TypeScript tests that do
# read it run on the host, never inside an image. Excluding it keeps the bundle out of every
# build context (decision 39).
tests/fixtures
# packages/sdk-js's `pnpm install` and `prepare` leave node_modules/ and dist/ that no Dockerfile COPYs
# (the SDK is a git dependency of its consumers, built on their side — sentinel-sdk-js contract §4.1 / D1).
packages/sdk-js/node_modules
packages/sdk-js/dist
